{
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/sarif-2.1/schema/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "fullName": "Trivy Vulnerability Scanner",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/aquasecurity/trivy",
          "name": "Trivy",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "DS-0001",
              "name": "Misconfiguration",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "':latest' tag used"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When using a 'FROM' statement you should use a specific tag to avoid uncontrolled behavior when the image is updated."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ds-0001",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration DS-0001\nType: Dockerfile Security Check\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nCheck: ':latest' tag used\nMessage: Specify a tag in the 'FROM' statement for image 'gcr.io/distroless/nodejs24-debian13'\nLink: [DS-0001](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ds-0001)\nWhen using a 'FROM' statement you should use a specific tag to avoid uncontrolled behavior when the image is updated.",
                "markdown": "**Misconfiguration DS-0001**\n| Type | Severity | Check | Message | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|Dockerfile Security Check|MEDIUM|':latest' tag used|Specify a tag in the 'FROM' statement for image 'gcr.io/distroless/nodejs24-debian13'|[DS-0001](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ds-0001)|\n\nWhen using a 'FROM' statement you should use a specific tag to avoid uncontrolled behavior when the image is updated."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "misconfiguration",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "DS-0026",
              "name": "Misconfiguration",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "No HEALTHCHECK defined"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "You should add HEALTHCHECK instruction in your docker container images to perform the health check on running containers."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ds-0026",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration DS-0026\nType: Dockerfile Security Check\nSeverity: LOW\nCheck: No HEALTHCHECK defined\nMessage: Add HEALTHCHECK instruction in your Dockerfile\nLink: [DS-0026](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ds-0026)\nYou should add HEALTHCHECK instruction in your docker container images to perform the health check on running containers.",
                "markdown": "**Misconfiguration DS-0026**\n| Type | Severity | Check | Message | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|Dockerfile Security Check|LOW|No HEALTHCHECK defined|Add HEALTHCHECK instruction in your Dockerfile|[DS-0026](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ds-0026)|\n\nYou should add HEALTHCHECK instruction in your docker container images to perform the health check on running containers."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "misconfiguration",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AWS-0017",
              "name": "Misconfiguration",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CloudWatch log groups should be encrypted using CMK"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CloudWatch log groups are encrypted by default, however, to get the full benefit of controlling key rotation and other KMS aspects a KMS CMK should be used.\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/aws-0017",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration AWS-0017\nType: Terraform Security Check\nSeverity: LOW\nCheck: CloudWatch log groups should be encrypted using CMK\nMessage: Log group is not encrypted.\nLink: [AWS-0017](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/aws-0017)\nCloudWatch log groups are encrypted by default, however, to get the full benefit of controlling key rotation and other KMS aspects a KMS CMK should be used.\n",
                "markdown": "**Misconfiguration AWS-0017**\n| Type | Severity | Check | Message | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|Terraform Security Check|LOW|CloudWatch log groups should be encrypted using CMK|Log group is not encrypted.|[AWS-0017](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/aws-0017)|\n\nCloudWatch log groups are encrypted by default, however, to get the full benefit of controlling key rotation and other KMS aspects a KMS CMK should be used.\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "misconfiguration",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AWS-0052",
              "name": "Misconfiguration",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Load balancers should drop invalid headers"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Passing unknown or invalid headers through to the target poses a potential risk of compromise.\nBy setting drop_invalid_header_fields to true, anything that does not conform to well known, defined headers will be removed by the load balancer.\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/aws-0052",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration AWS-0052\nType: Terraform Security Check\nSeverity: HIGH\nCheck: Load balancers should drop invalid headers\nMessage: Application load balancer is not set to drop invalid headers.\nLink: [AWS-0052](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/aws-0052)\nPassing unknown or invalid headers through to the target poses a potential risk of compromise.\nBy setting drop_invalid_header_fields to true, anything that does not conform to well known, defined headers will be removed by the load balancer.\n",
                "markdown": "**Misconfiguration AWS-0052**\n| Type | Severity | Check | Message | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|Terraform Security Check|HIGH|Load balancers should drop invalid headers|Application load balancer is not set to drop invalid headers.|[AWS-0052](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/aws-0052)|\n\nPassing unknown or invalid headers through to the target poses a potential risk of compromise.\nBy setting drop_invalid_header_fields to true, anything that does not conform to well known, defined headers will be removed by the load balancer.\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "misconfiguration",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AWS-0053",
              "name": "Misconfiguration",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Load balancer is exposed to the internet."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "There are many scenarios in which you would want to expose a load balancer to the wider internet, but this check exists as a warning to prevent accidental exposure of internal assets. You should ensure that this resource should be exposed publicly.\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/aws-0053",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration AWS-0053\nType: Terraform Security Check\nSeverity: HIGH\nCheck: Load balancer is exposed to the internet.\nMessage: Load balancer is exposed publicly.\nLink: [AWS-0053](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/aws-0053)\nThere are many scenarios in which you would want to expose a load balancer to the wider internet, but this check exists as a warning to prevent accidental exposure of internal assets. You should ensure that this resource should be exposed publicly.\n",
                "markdown": "**Misconfiguration AWS-0053**\n| Type | Severity | Check | Message | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|Terraform Security Check|HIGH|Load balancer is exposed to the internet.|Load balancer is exposed publicly.|[AWS-0053](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/aws-0053)|\n\nThere are many scenarios in which you would want to expose a load balancer to the wider internet, but this check exists as a warning to prevent accidental exposure of internal assets. You should ensure that this resource should be exposed publicly.\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "misconfiguration",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AWS-0054",
              "name": "Misconfiguration",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Use of plain HTTP."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Plain HTTP is unencrypted and human-readable. This means that if a malicious actor was to eavesdrop on your connection, they would be able to see all of your data flowing back and forth.\nYou should use HTTPS, which is HTTP over an encrypted (TLS) connection, meaning eavesdroppers cannot read your traffic.\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/aws-0054",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration AWS-0054\nType: Terraform Security Check\nSeverity: CRITICAL\nCheck: Use of plain HTTP.\nMessage: Listener for application load balancer does not use HTTPS.\nLink: [AWS-0054](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/aws-0054)\nPlain HTTP is unencrypted and human-readable. This means that if a malicious actor was to eavesdrop on your connection, they would be able to see all of your data flowing back and forth.\nYou should use HTTPS, which is HTTP over an encrypted (TLS) connection, meaning eavesdroppers cannot read your traffic.\n",
                "markdown": "**Misconfiguration AWS-0054**\n| Type | Severity | Check | Message | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|Terraform Security Check|CRITICAL|Use of plain HTTP.|Listener for application load balancer does not use HTTPS.|[AWS-0054](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/aws-0054)|\n\nPlain HTTP is unencrypted and human-readable. This means that if a malicious actor was to eavesdrop on your connection, they would be able to see all of your data flowing back and forth.\nYou should use HTTPS, which is HTTP over an encrypted (TLS) connection, meaning eavesdroppers cannot read your traffic.\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "9.5",
                "tags": [
                  "misconfiguration",
                  "security",
                  "CRITICAL"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AWS-0104",
              "name": "Misconfiguration",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "A security group rule should not allow unrestricted egress to any IP address."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Opening up ports to connect out to the public internet is generally to be avoided. You should restrict access to IP addresses or ranges that are explicitly required where possible.\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/aws-0104",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration AWS-0104\nType: Terraform Security Check\nSeverity: CRITICAL\nCheck: A security group rule should not allow unrestricted egress to any IP address.\nMessage: Security group rule allows unrestricted egress to any IP address.\nLink: [AWS-0104](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/aws-0104)\nOpening up ports to connect out to the public internet is generally to be avoided. You should restrict access to IP addresses or ranges that are explicitly required where possible.\n",
                "markdown": "**Misconfiguration AWS-0104**\n| Type | Severity | Check | Message | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|Terraform Security Check|CRITICAL|A security group rule should not allow unrestricted egress to any IP address.|Security group rule allows unrestricted egress to any IP address.|[AWS-0104](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/aws-0104)|\n\nOpening up ports to connect out to the public internet is generally to be avoided. You should restrict access to IP addresses or ranges that are explicitly required where possible.\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "9.5",
                "tags": [
                  "misconfiguration",
                  "security",
                  "CRITICAL"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AWS-0124",
              "name": "Misconfiguration",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Missing description for security group rule."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Security group rules should include a description for auditing purposes.\n\nSimplifies auditing, debugging, and managing security groups.\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/aws-0124",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration AWS-0124\nType: Terraform Security Check\nSeverity: LOW\nCheck: Missing description for security group rule.\nMessage: Security group rule does not have a description.\nLink: [AWS-0124](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/aws-0124)\nSecurity group rules should include a description for auditing purposes.\n\nSimplifies auditing, debugging, and managing security groups.\n",
                "markdown": "**Misconfiguration AWS-0124**\n| Type | Severity | Check | Message | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|Terraform Security Check|LOW|Missing description for security group rule.|Security group rule does not have a description.|[AWS-0124](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/aws-0124)|\n\nSecurity group rules should include a description for auditing purposes.\n\nSimplifies auditing, debugging, and managing security groups.\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "misconfiguration",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AWS-0164",
              "name": "Misconfiguration",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Instances in a subnet should not receive a public IP address by default."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "You should limit the provision of public IP addresses for resources. Resources should not be exposed on the public internet, but should have access limited to consumers required for the function of your application.\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/aws-0164",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration AWS-0164\nType: Terraform Security Check\nSeverity: HIGH\nCheck: Instances in a subnet should not receive a public IP address by default.\nMessage: Subnet associates public IP address.\nLink: [AWS-0164](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/aws-0164)\nYou should limit the provision of public IP addresses for resources. Resources should not be exposed on the public internet, but should have access limited to consumers required for the function of your application.\n",
                "markdown": "**Misconfiguration AWS-0164**\n| Type | Severity | Check | Message | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|Terraform Security Check|HIGH|Instances in a subnet should not receive a public IP address by default.|Subnet associates public IP address.|[AWS-0164](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/aws-0164)|\n\nYou should limit the provision of public IP addresses for resources. Resources should not be exposed on the public internet, but should have access limited to consumers required for the function of your application.\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "misconfiguration",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AWS-0178",
              "name": "Misconfiguration",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "VPC Flow Logs is a feature that enables you to capture information about the IP traffic going to and from network interfaces in your VPC. After you've created a flow log, you can view and retrieve its data in Amazon CloudWatch Logs. It is recommended that VPC Flow Logs be enabled for packet \"Rejects\" for VPCs."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "VPC Flow Logs provide visibility into network traffic that traverses the VPC and can be used to detect anomalous traffic or insight during security workflows.\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/aws-0178",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration AWS-0178\nType: Terraform Security Check\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nCheck: VPC Flow Logs is a feature that enables you to capture information about the IP traffic going to and from network interfaces in your VPC. After you've created a flow log, you can view and retrieve its data in Amazon CloudWatch Logs. It is recommended that VPC Flow Logs be enabled for packet \"Rejects\" for VPCs.\nMessage: VPC does not have VPC Flow Logs enabled.\nLink: [AWS-0178](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/aws-0178)\nVPC Flow Logs provide visibility into network traffic that traverses the VPC and can be used to detect anomalous traffic or insight during security workflows.\n",
                "markdown": "**Misconfiguration AWS-0178**\n| Type | Severity | Check | Message | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|Terraform Security Check|MEDIUM|VPC Flow Logs is a feature that enables you to capture information about the IP traffic going to and from network interfaces in your VPC. After you've created a flow log, you can view and retrieve its data in Amazon CloudWatch Logs. It is recommended that VPC Flow Logs be enabled for packet \"Rejects\" for VPCs.|VPC does not have VPC Flow Logs enabled.|[AWS-0178](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/aws-0178)|\n\nVPC Flow Logs provide visibility into network traffic that traverses the VPC and can be used to detect anomalous traffic or insight during security workflows.\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "misconfiguration",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "private-key",
              "name": "Secret",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Asymmetric Private Key"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "----BEGIN RSA PRIVATE KEY-----************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************-----END RSA PRIVATE"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/aquasecurity/trivy/blob/main/pkg/fanal/secret/builtin-rules.go",
              "help": {
                "text": "Secret Asymmetric Private Key\nSeverity: HIGH\nMatch: ----BEGIN RSA PRIVATE KEY-----************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************-----END RSA PRIVATE",
                "markdown": "**Secret Asymmetric Private Key**\n| Severity | Match |\n| --- | --- |\n|HIGH|----BEGIN RSA PRIVATE KEY-----************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************-----END RSA PRIVATE|"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "secret",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "version": "0.76.2"
        }
